{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088154-incarnation-and-banality-for-c20-dark-kin","id":1088154,"title":"Incarnation and Banality for C20 Dark-Kin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-05T02:08:25-07:00","id":1088154,"title":"Incarnation and Banality for C20 Dark-Kin","content":"Well, I understand wordcount limitations for the corebook all too well, but I was under the distinct impression that all the faerie breeds included in the corebook (Kithain, Gallain, Inanimae, Thallain, and Dark-Kin) were intended to be playable. Yet, I find the rules for the Dark-Kin to operate in the Autumn World and deal with Banality sketchy to the point of being hardly usable for PC. Can someone explain in a bit more depth how possessing mortals or physically manifesting as incarnate spirits work for them, and how they deal with Banality if they do so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T14:59:53-07:00","id":1088866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088154-incarnation-and-banality-for-c20-dark-kin#post1088154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I understand wordcount limitations for the corebook all too well, but I was under the distinct impression that all the faerie breeds included in the corebook (Kithain, Gallain, Inanimae, Thallain, and Dark-Kin) were intended to be playable. Yet, I find the rules for the Dark-Kin to operate in the Autumn World and deal with Banality sketchy to the point of being hardly usable for PC. Can someone explain in a bit more depth how possessing mortals or physically manifesting as incarnate spirits work for them, and how they deal with Banality if they do so?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, all the Gallain are better served by their original write-ups. In this case, in Denizens of the Dreaming. The Gallain got very short shrift in C20 compared to the huge bulk of clans in V20. This book could've been 100 pages longer with all the stuff in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T15:25:18-07:00","id":1088879,"title":"","content":"Word counts were tight. The Gallain write-ups aren't meant to completely replace the books they appear in - just introduce them to folks who don't know them and give just enough information to play them while cleaning up the rules were necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T15:36:11-07:00","id":1088881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088154-incarnation-and-banality-for-c20-dark-kin?p=1088866#post1088866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, all the Gallain are better served by their original write-ups. In this case, in Denizens of the Dreaming. The Gallain got very short shrift in C20 compared to the huge bulk of clans in V20. This book could've been 100 pages longer with all the stuff in it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel like the Hsien alchemies are more clearly written up in this than in 8million dreams, but that's probably because of Pillars in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T16:59:42-07:00","id":1088906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1088154-incarnation-and-banality-for-c20-dark-kin?p=1088879#post1088879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Word counts were tight. The Gallain write-ups aren't meant to completely replace the books they appear in - just introduce them to folks who don't know them and give just enough information to play them while cleaning up the rules were necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the word-count problem, really. My own is the Dark-kin rules in C20 for physical manifestation/incarnation or possession of mortals and dealing with Banality read fuzzy and sketchy to the point of being hardly playable, and their equivalents in Denizens of the Dreaming different enough to be hardly compatible and usable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}